on Kyber server rack was running into delays. CNBC cites the report as context for the divergence between Nvidia shares and the broader chip-sector sell-off.\\n    Quote: Shares of Nvidia fought into the green despite a 5% sell-off in chip stocks tracked by the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (SMH) , a notable outperformance a day after a research report claiming the AI leader was at least a year behind on manufacturing of its next line of server racks. … Similar action took place in Nvidia Monday after the company disputed a report by SemiAnalysis that its next-gen Kyber\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e211 [party_statement; cnbc.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:b48593184704bbbe6eddbc03 2026-07-07] Nvidia disputed a SemiAnalysis report that its next-generation Kyber server rack was running into delays, i.e., the company pushed back on the claim that its Kyber product schedule had slipped. The dispute came on a Monday, per CNBC.\\n    Quote: Similar action took place in Nvidia Monday after the company disputed a report by SemiAnalysis that its next-gen Kyber server rack was running into delays.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e194 (); both are in force: The item reports that the Kyber delay applies only to the Rubin Ultra phase and its Kyber rack, and that Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, are not part of the reported delay.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St. (citing CNBC citing SemiAnalysis); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Semiconductor research firm SemiAnalysis reported on July 5–6, 2026 (cited by CNBC) that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed from a planned 2027 launch to 2028, with the gating item a 78-layer PCB midplane (which NVIDIA calls the orthogonal backplane) that SemiAnalysis said 'remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint.'\\n    Quote: Semiconductor research firm SemiAnalysis reported on July 5–6, 2026 that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed, from its planned 2027 launch to 2028. CNBC cited the SemiAnalysis post. … The reported culprit is a component most retail investors have not heard of: the PCB midplane (which NVIDIA also calls the orthogonal backplane), a printed circuit board with up to 78 layers t\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson (via Bloomberg); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA publicly disputed SemiAnalysis's Kyber NVL144 delay report, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg that the company's 'roadmap is intact.' The item notes NVIDIA has not confirmed the delay.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.” … NVIDIA has not confirmed the delay.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e223 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St. (citing SemiAnalysis); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA's larger NVL576 rack system — designed to link eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small initial volumes.\\n    Quote: A larger sibling, the NVL576, designed to link eight racks via optical connections, is also likely delayed or limited to small initial volumes, according to SemiAnalysis.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e97; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e258 [third_party_view; futuriom.com (citing a SemiAnalysis X post); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] This week, research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks. The article says this could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson (via futuriom.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson responded that \\\"Our road map is intact\\\" and that \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline,\\\" reaffirming the company's schedule in the face of the reported Kyber manufacturing setbacks.\\n    Quote: An NVIDIA spokesperson said, “Our road map is intact.” Further, \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e133 (); both are in force: SemiAnalysis separately reported about a week earlier that Nvidia had cancelled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favour of a two-chiplet design, also citing \\\"manufacturing execution concerns\\\"; the two-die offering will deliver around half the performance of the four-die Rubin Ultra.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; CNBC, citing SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture (Kyber NVL144), designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips and slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The design mounts graphics processing units in compute trays that sit vertically instead of ho\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e113, e129, e174, e178, e182, e187, e189, e210, e221, e307; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's report of the Kyber delay, stating that \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115, e132, e179, e193, e211, e222, e338; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson (via futuriom.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson responded that \\\"Our road map is intact\\\" and that \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline,\\\" reaffirming the company's schedule in the face of the reported Kyber manufacturing setbacks.\\n    Quote: An NVIDIA spokesperson said, “Our road map is intact.” Further, \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e308, e322; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e133 (); both are in force: SemiAnalysis separately reported about a week earlier that Nvidia had cancelled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favour of a two-chiplet design, also citing \\\"manufacturing execution concerns\\\"; the two-die offering will deliver around half the performance of the four-die Rubin Ultra.\",\n   \"- e307 [rumour; barchart.com (citing reports); original source  ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia faced recent reports suggesting its next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure, designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, could be delayed until 2028 rather than launching in 2027 as expected.\\n    Quote: Recently, Nvidia faced reports that suggested its next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure could be delayed until 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e308 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia Corporation ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia denied the speculation that Kyber is delayed, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track; the item states Kyber, designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system.\\n    Quote: However, the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key component of Nvidia's long-term AI infrastructure strategy.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e259; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e258 (); both are in force: This week, research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks. The article says this could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model.\",\n   \"- e322 [party_statement; IEEE Spectrum (Knvul Sheikh); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] Nvidia is planning to add more processors to single interconnected systems, moving from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027, IEEE Spectrum reports.\\n    Quote: At the same time, Nvidia is planning to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e259; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e338 [party_statement; moomoo.com (relaying Nvidia's statement to Bloomberg); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Nvidia said in a recent statement to Bloomberg that it denies claims of a technical delay and that its product roadmap remains intact; the item does not specify which product or delay claim the denial addresses.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e258 (); both are in force: This week, research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks. The article says this could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's report of the Kyber delay, stating that \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115, e132, e179, e193, e211, e222, e338, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e258 [third_party_view; futuriom.com (citing a SemiAnalysis X post); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] This week, research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks. The article says this could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e387; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e387 [rumour; Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] Reports circulated that NVIDIA's next-generation AI chips — specifically the Kyber platform — are being delayed, cited as the reason NVIDIA is in the news; in the quoted discussion the delay claim is attributed to SemiAnalysis, which said 'everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.' The report is unconfirmed and contested (NVIDIA denies it).\\n    Quote: AI giant NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is currently in the news these days due to reports of a delay to its next generation AI chips. … You know Semi Analysis does pretty good work, saying that everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e258; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e388 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com); original source NVIDIA Corp. ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] NVIDIA officially denied reports that its Kyber platform is being delayed, disputing the reported schedule slip.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; CNBC, citing SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture (Kyber NVL144), designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips and slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The design mounts graphics processing units in compute trays that sit vertically instead of ho\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e113, e129, e174, e178, e182, e187, e189, e210, e221, e307, e426; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's report of the Kyber delay, stating that \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e115, e132, e179, e193, e211, e222, e338, e388, e427; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e426 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] The technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of difficulties manufacturing a crucial circuit board. The report is framed as a possible delay, not a confirmed schedule change.\\n    Quote: technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e427 [party_statement; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Nvidia said its product roadmap remains intact, in response to SemiAnalysis's reported possibility that the Kyber NVL144 rack system could slip to 2028; the article notes questions linger despite the company's statement.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e436 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture, as part of an effort to reassure investors that its AI product roadmap is on track.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e96 (); both are in force: Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture (Kyber NVL144), designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips and slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system remains difficult to manufacture.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; CNBC, citing SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture (Kyber NVL144), designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips and slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the multi-layer PCB midplane at the heart of the system remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The design mounts graphics processing units in compute trays that sit vertically instead of ho\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e113, e129, e174, e178, e182, e187, e189, e210, e221, e307, e426, e538; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson (via futuriom.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] An NVIDIA spokesperson responded that \\\"Our road map is intact\\\" and that \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline,\\\" reaffirming the company's schedule in the face of the reported Kyber manufacturing setbacks.\\n    Quote: An NVIDIA spokesperson said, “Our road map is intact.” Further, \\\"Vera Rubin Ultra will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e308, e322, e539; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e133 (); both are in force: SemiAnalysis separately reported about a week earlier that Nvidia had cancelled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favour of a two-chiplet design, also citing \\\"manufacturing execution concerns\\\"; the two-die offering will deliver around half the performance of the four-die Rubin Ultra.\",\n   \"- e538 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Industry research firm SemiAnalysis reported over the weekend before 2026-07-14 that Nvidia's upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028; the article presents this as reports/rumours circulating rather than a confirmed schedule change.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia’s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e539 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson countered reports of delays to its upcoming architectures, saying the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" after SemiAnalysis report of a possible Kyber NVL144 delay into 2028.\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e259; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 4,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Vera Rubin platform by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether Nvidia begins shipping its Vera Rubin platform by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Vera Rubin by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Vera Rubin by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i105\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i202\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\",\n     \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i207\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\",\n     \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e26 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source fool.com analyst Justin Pope 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\",\n   \"- e61 [rumour; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems were reported to be in full production and scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n   \"- e64 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] Nvidia plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU as part of the Vera Rubin platform in fall 2026.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\",\n   \"- e61 [rumour; CNBC; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems were reported to be in full production and scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e145; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e83 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated the Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack would cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, versus about $4 million for the GB300 NVL72.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.\",\n   \"- e84 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated Nvidia would charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU in volume sales.\\n    Quote: The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n   \"- e85 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory content in each Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, up 435% from the prior generation, including 54 terabytes of LPDDR5X and roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n   \"- e86 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] MarketScale reported that first Vera Rubin rack shipments were scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4 2026.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n   \"- e87 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory’s share of the VR200 bill of materials at 25–30%, versus 5–10% for GB200, while the GPU share fell from about 63% to 51%.\\n    Quote: As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\",\n   \"- e104 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source 247WallSt.com 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author reports delays across NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems, without specifying a revised schedule.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e145 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s Rubin systems were reported to be in full production and scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: That’s likely because the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e61; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e176 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] Nvidia said in March that it plans to launch the Vera Rubin Space-1 Module in the future; no launch date was specified.\\n    Quote: Nvidia announced in March that it will be launching its Vera Rubin Space-1 Module at some point in the future.\",\n   \"- e202 [party_statement; straitstimes.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia is working to release its Rubin chip lineup in the second half of 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is now working to release an even more powerful line-up called Rubin in the second half of 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e176 (); both are in force: Nvidia said in March that it plans to launch the Vera Rubin Space-1 Module in the future; no launch date was specified.\",\n   \"- e271 [party_statement; moomoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA denied claims of a technical delay and said its product roadmap remains intact; the item does not identify a specific product or shipment date.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e104 (2026-07-06); both are in force: The author reports delays across NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems, without specifying a revised schedule.\",\n   \"- e346 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e176 (); both are in force: Nvidia said in March that it plans to launch the Vera Rubin Space-1 Module in the future; no launch date was specified.\",\n   \"- e348 [rumour; en.sedaily.com, reporting information attributed to the semiconductor industry; original source en.sedaily.com (unnamed-source report) ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] Unnamed semiconductor-industry sources reported that LG completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in 1H 2026 and plans reliability evaluations in 2H, then global customer orders and mass production in 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
